<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1106">1106</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf ibn Tashfin was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> who died in 1106. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> as the Almoravid capital, completed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and, at the invitation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kings, intervened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sagrajas">Sagrajas</a> in 1086. He later deposed the taifa rulers and brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> under direct Almoravid rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin.jpg" alt="Yusuf ibn Tashfin" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yusuf_Ben_Tasfin_dinar_22562.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
